/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  filter05_calciumSilicate_measuredTest

  A SAMPLE'S BEHAVIOUR FROM ITS RAW TEST ROWS, held to the printed worked
  example of Wakeman & Tarleton, Solid/Liquid Separation: Principles of
  Industrial Filtration (2005), Example 4.1, pp. 121-123 (after Hosseini
  1977): a calcium silicate suspension in a laboratory filter press, 69 kPa,
  0.0429 m2, s = 0.0495, m_av = 3.405, and the eleven t-V rows of Table 4.9.

  WHERE THE NUMBERS LIVE (docs/design/measured-facts-materials-and-flow-
  curves.md R6): the unit carries no resistance.  `sample` names
  constant/experiments/calciumSilicate_hosseini1977_69kPa.dat, a record of
  kind `measured` holding the ROWS; the service fits the line t/V against V
  through the linear region (the first two points disregarded, as the book
  does) and answers alpha and R_m at this pressure, with its method and its
  support status, printed in the run.
  THE BOOK'S ANSWERS (pp. 122-123): alpha = 7.4e9 m/kg, R_m = 1.54e10 1/m.
  The least squares through the same rows gives 7.43e9 and 1.538e10 (the
  book prints its regression's intercept rounded: 5186 against 5197 s/m3);
  the anchors below carry the 1 % band that covers the book's rounding.
  WHAT IS NOT THE BOOK'S: the cycle (the book's test has no cleaning time:
  10 min is illustrative), the feed rate (set to about one press), the water's
  viscosity and density (the package's: 8.89e-4 Pa s and 996.9 kg/m3, against
  the test's 0.001 and 1000), and the solid: a case-local pseudo-solid of the
  test's 1950 kg/m3 density (MW 100 is a BASIS, no result depends on it).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
application   choupoSolve;
description   "A laboratory filter press on a calcium silicate suspension whose cake resistance is DERIVED from the raw t-V rows of a measured test (Wakeman & Tarleton Example 4.1): alpha and R_m, with the method and the support status printed.";
verbosity     3;
citations
(
    "Wakeman, R.J.; Tarleton, E.S. (2005) Solid/Liquid Separation: Principles of Industrial Filtration. Elsevier. Chapter 4, Example 4.1, Tables 4.8 and 4.9, pp. 121-123 (after Hosseini 1977)."
);
